  "discussion": {
    "headline": "October to kick off on unseasonably warm and muggy note",
    "dateLine": "10:30 a.m. Tuesday, September 29, 2026",
    "excerpt": "As expected, the Nor'easter spoiled outdoor plans across central and eastern PA during the last weekend of September. Gusty winds, showers and bands of steadier rain rotated around the backside of the system from northeast-to-southwest across the region. Rainfall amounts gradually increased from west-to-east and ranged from 0.25\" or less in parts of Franklin and Adams Counties to over 2\" in Philadelphia (see below). …",
